WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:01.910
Alright, so big announcement.

00:00:01.910 --> 00:00:03.590
Sam Harris is going to be on the program.

00:00:03.590 --> 00:00:06.569
The interview has actually already been recorded.

00:00:06.569 --> 00:00:10.530
Announce it before it got recorded because
uh, I wanted to make sure that it actually

00:00:10.530 --> 00:00:12.200
was going to happen to be totally honest.

00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:17.200
And sometimes these things can get moved around
when the guest is a very busy person as is

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:26.160
Sam, the genesis of the interview is that
I guess people in Sam's audience told him

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:31.210
that he should appear on my show and he got
in touch and we set it up.

00:00:31.210 --> 00:00:36.170
There were no guidelines put in place in terms
of what topics should be discussed or anything

00:00:36.170 --> 00:00:37.170
like that.

00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:38.829
I was free to ask anything I wanted.

00:00:38.829 --> 00:00:43.629
And the plan is we're going to publish some
short clips over the weekend and then the

00:00:43.629 --> 00:00:45.949
entire interview will air next week.

00:00:45.949 --> 00:00:47.760
It's a nearly hour and a half interview.

00:00:47.760 --> 00:00:51.780
So there's a practical question about how
to include it in the broadcast shows.

00:00:51.780 --> 00:00:56.870
We can either take almost two entire whole
shows, a significant portion of two shows

00:00:56.870 --> 00:00:58.100
in a row.

00:00:58.100 --> 00:01:02.159
We could split it into four pieces and do
one piece Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday.

00:01:02.159 --> 00:01:03.609
That's another possibility.

00:01:03.609 --> 00:01:08.570
In any case, the full nearly 90 minute interview
is going to be posted in its entirety without

00:01:08.570 --> 00:01:13.409
any edits, cuts or whatever on youtube sometime
next week as well.

00:01:13.409 --> 00:01:17.119
But I'm open to hearing from you about how
we should manage it on the show.

00:01:17.119 --> 00:01:23.960
Some of the things that we discussed, Sam
Harris had an interesting take on how he compares

00:01:23.960 --> 00:01:30.079
and contrasts Donald Trump and Osama bin Laden,
which you might be surprised to hear is a

00:01:30.079 --> 00:01:33.570
comparison anybody would be making, but that
was discussed.

00:01:33.570 --> 00:01:37.679
Uh, Sam Harris had some interesting thoughts
about Trump voters.

00:01:37.679 --> 00:01:41.729
We talked about allegations of racism against
Donald Trump.

00:01:41.729 --> 00:01:47.409
Um, Sam gave his views on the media landscape
including his thoughts on Fox News.

00:01:47.409 --> 00:01:55.350
We got into guns and the sort of culture and
religion of guns as Sam Harris described it.

00:01:55.350 --> 00:02:00.429
There was an open borders discussion about
immigration policy where we had some disagreements

00:02:00.429 --> 00:02:02.549
and some agreements.

00:02:02.549 --> 00:02:09.080
Sam Harris talked about reparations, which
he finds, uh, something that he would likely

00:02:09.080 --> 00:02:12.900
support after, uh, looking at detailed plans
for it.

00:02:12.900 --> 00:02:18.150
But believes is a strategic mistake for Democrats
to be talking about going into 2020 we talked

00:02:18.150 --> 00:02:24.490
about uh, terrorist manifestos where I found
what I believed was a double standard in some

00:02:24.490 --> 00:02:26.380
of the things Sam Harris had said.

00:02:26.380 --> 00:02:27.380
We talked about that.

00:02:27.380 --> 00:02:31.610
Now, my only concern, and I'm sharing kind
of a lot here about the behind the scenes.

00:02:31.610 --> 00:02:35.140
This was a 90 minute interview and Sam Harris
has a lot to say about a lot of different

00:02:35.140 --> 00:02:36.140
things.

00:02:36.140 --> 00:02:44.930
Whenever I do an interview like this, I always
come away feeling as though I could have totally

00:02:44.930 --> 00:02:50.480
prevented the interview from moving forward
by arguing to the end.

00:02:50.480 --> 00:02:56.260
Every single disagreement that I have with
the guest, and it's just not a practical way

00:02:56.260 --> 00:03:01.560
to do the interview, but every time I do this,
I know that there was going to be some portion

00:03:01.560 --> 00:03:06.170
of the audience who will write to me and they'll
say, David, the guests said x.

00:03:06.170 --> 00:03:08.150
How did you not challenge that?

00:03:08.150 --> 00:03:10.230
It makes you seem complicit.

00:03:10.230 --> 00:03:15.480
And I hope my, my real hope with the Sam Harris
interview, particularly since he was very

00:03:15.480 --> 00:03:21.790
generous with his time, is that people don't
come away focused on wow, well you talked

00:03:21.790 --> 00:03:27.070
about these 10 things on these two, you should
have just pushed back, pushed back, pushed

00:03:27.070 --> 00:03:28.090
back.

00:03:28.090 --> 00:03:32.810
There's a practical nature to these things
where if I want to torpedo the interview and

00:03:32.810 --> 00:03:35.940
prevent it from moving forward, I can do that.

00:03:35.940 --> 00:03:37.620
But at some point it doesn't make practical
sense.

00:03:37.620 --> 00:03:39.260
This has happened when I've interviewed academics.

00:03:39.260 --> 00:03:41.850
This has happened when I've interviewed extremists
like Richard Spencer.

00:03:41.850 --> 00:03:46.260
Um, so that is something I, I've sort of been
thinking about since the interview was filmed.

00:03:46.260 --> 00:03:50.690
So Sam Harris interview some clips on Youtube
over the weekend full thing next week.

